{
  "_id": "90eaf5457b7cfa8f",
  "name": "Tides of War",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "icons/magic/water/ice-crystal-white.webp",
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you gain the ability, you learn that you can grab and weaponize water, and how to make a trident's strike especially deadly.</p>\n<p>You learn the Water Flow trick, using either your Strength or Dexterity modifier as the creative ability modifier.</p>\n<p>As an action, you can grab water and fire it as a blast in the form of a line that is (Your proficiency bonus x 20) long, and 5ft wide. All creatures within this line must make a Dexterity Saving Throw, DC equal to 8 + your Strength or Dexterity modifier + your Proficiency Bonus. On a failure, they take your (proficiency bonus)d10 bludgeoning damage and half on a success.</p>\n<p>You can use this feature 3 times per long rest.</p>\n<p>In addition, while wielding a trident, the size of the damage dice increases by one size.</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
